WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.420
In this upcoming meditation exercise, we are going to learn a repeatable technique for starting our sits.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:13.760
We're first going to work on setting up the posture for a seated meditation,

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:18.580
which can be really helpful for not having too much discomfort while we're meditating.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:26.920
And then we'll go through a breathing progression that can be a really nice way to transition from not meditating to meditating.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:33.330
One of the reasons we really like to introduce this technique on the first day is that it

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:38.520
can be helpful to have a repeatable technique that you use every time you start a meditation.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:46.740
It can decrease the amount of trying to figure out what to do or how to do and make it really easy to transition into sitting.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:54.140
And also, sometimes when people try out a technique right at the beginning of meditation, it doesn't always work.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:58.360
and one thing that's really helpful is just knowing if you take a little bit of time,

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.340
let yourself settle a little bit, and then try that technique again,

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.440
it often can impact you differently throughout the meditation.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.380
And this means that even if the technique doesn't work right away,

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.560
you don't have to abandon it entirely, but just let the meditation continue progressing

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.220
and it might start working differently in a little bit.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:24.860
To help explore that part, I'm going to ask you as we do this to a number of times throughout

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:28.560
this exercise, take three breaths and then smile.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:35.080
And as we're doing the exercise, just try and notice what is the difference when I do

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:40.720
this same movement of taking three breaths and smiling at the beginning, and then how

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:46.400
does that same movement change after I've set up the posture, and then how is it again

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:53.660
after we've gone through a breathing progression. So just to settle in you can

00:01:54.360 --> 00:02:00.360
find a seated posture that to start is gonna allow you to settle in and then

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.400
I'll take us through setting up that posture.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:15.180
So as we begin this meditation I want you to start by just taking three deep

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:23.120
breaths in and out through your nose and then noticing what it feels like to put

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.360
a smile on your face.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:06.600
And then after the three breaths, just take a moment to see if there's a smile that might be available.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.260
And seeing how it feels to smile.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:24.960
And just making a quick mental note of what that felt like so that we can return to that when we do the same movement later.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:36.340
So to set up the posture for meditation, the first thing that you want to do is make sure that your hips are above your knees.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.960
If your hips are below your knees, then you'll really start to sink

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:46.920
into them, and that'll cause constriction. That'll later cause pain in your back.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:52.500
So, if you're seated, it can be helpful to put a cushion underneath you to help

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:57.620
raise your hips up, or you can just extend out your feet a little bit, and that

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:02.740
can often make it so that the knees are equal to a level than the hips.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:20.760
After you've made that adjustment, just taking a moment to bring your awareness to your legs.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:28.420
And notice if there are any obvious places that your legs feel agitated or tight.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:37.760
Just seeing if you can let your legs spread out and let your legs form a solid base for the rest of your body.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:56.980
And now know that we've set the legs up and they should be in a position where they won't bother us for the rest of the meditation.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.160
And next you can bring awareness to your lower back.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:10.460
And just notice if that area feels tight or slouched anyway.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:23.660
And just gently see if you can feel the top of your head slowly, gently have a slight tug upwards.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:27.020
Nothing that's introducing more tension.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:35.280
but just a way of breathing, bringing a little bit more space into the whole body.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.380
And you might also feel your sit bones rooting down

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:46.740
and just feeling space along the whole body.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:06.880
And next you can bring awareness to your hands and just have them resting gently in your lap, face up or face down.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:20.420
And on your in-breath, you can bring your fists, make your hands into fists. And then on your out-breath, let them relax.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:31.580
Next, bringing awareness to your chest and upper back.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:36.640
And on your in-breath, you can bring your shoulders up to your ears.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:50.280
And then on your out-breath, just slowly and gently let them drift down and almost feel them just slot into place.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:04.180
Next, you can bring awareness to the place where the back of your neck meets your skull.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.480
And just notice if it feels tight there at all.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.140
And it can be helpful to just gently tuck your chin.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:30.900
to help make sure that our body is vertically stacked we'll do a couple of sways so to start

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:38.340
we'll just sway forward and then backward and just you can start with a bigger swing

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:44.140
and then slowly work your way down to a smaller and smaller swing.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:56.280
And just see if you can find a place where it feels like your whole body is aligned vertically.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.680
And then you can do the same thing left to right.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:30.780
Letting your posture continue to deepen, continue to settle.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:50.800
Just finding an alignment that feels supportive, relaxed, open.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.960
Next, you can bring awareness to your mouth.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.320
Just see if you can let your jaw relax.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:08.000
Let your tongue relax.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:27.140
Bring awareness to your eyes and see if you can just behind your eyelids let your eyes soften.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:40.060
Maybe just letting your whole head relax.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.960
And now bringing your awareness to your whole body.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:55.040
just knowing that we set up the posture

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:59.160
for you to be relaxed and stable

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.100
and aligned

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:07.160
and that naturally throughout the rest of the sit

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.300
your body will continue to move

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:14.160
continue to shift, continue to change

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:20.800
And there's no need to feel like you have to be completely exactly still.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:27.100
But just letting your body open and unfold and deepen.

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:41.100
And within this supported and aligned posture.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:51.440
Just taking a moment now to take three deep breaths and then see what it would feel like to smile.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:54.600
And just noticing how that experience of smiling was different from the first one.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.800
Was there any more softness?

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:04.640
Any more openness?

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.740
Did you relate to it any differently?

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:33.540
And now I'm going to take us through a breathing progression.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:40.020
So start by feeling the breath in your abdomen.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:46.520
Just be aware that the body is breathing.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:13:01.440
See if there's any ability to feel comforted or at ease or soothed by the fact that the

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:02.280
body is breathing.

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:27.320
And feeling your breath in your stomach, we're slowly going to add feeling the breath in more and more parts of our body.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:38.120
So now see if you can feel the breath in your stomach and in your side abdomen.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:47.280
and just being very relaxed and easeful as you do so.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:57.040
But just a general sense of feeling the breath across your whole front and side abdomen.

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:12.560
And now you can add in your lower back as well.

00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:23.960
So feeling the breath on all four sides of your body in that same area.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:43.540
and not needing to have a very precise form of attention

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:50.100
but a very soft, gentle, tender awareness

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:57.220
Just a sense that the breath is moving in and out of those areas.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:08.220
And if you notice that it feels hard or difficult in any way, just see if you can let yourself

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:08.680
relax.

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:39.440
And next I want you to see if you can add in the area up to your ribs.

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:48.460
So just feeling the breath from the bottom of your ribs down to your hips.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.820
and all four sides of your body.

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:32.360
And next you can add in your hips as well.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.420
So your hip flexors and your glutes.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:49.740
Just feeling those areas slightly expand on your in-breath.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:55.980
and then feeling them get a little bit more relaxed on your out breath.

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:44.900
And next we can add in our upper legs, so our hamstrings and our quads down to our knees.

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:57.700
So just a very gentle sense that when you take an in-breath, those areas slightly, if

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.660
only marginally, expand as well.

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:26.180
And just seeing if you can make your awareness of the breath in these areas.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:31.080
Very soft, very tender, very caring.

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:54.360
And next you can add in the chest and the upper back.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:09.680
Feeling the breath fill the whole torso and the hamstrings and the quads.

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:33.260
Next, you can add in your lower leg.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:41.920
so your shins, your calves, your ankles, and your feet.

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:53.780
Just feeling with each in-breath, even your toes being energized and expanding.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:20.100
And you can also add in your arms, your upper arm, your forearm, your hands, each and every

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:20.500
finger.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:28.760
So just feeling into everything that is below your neck.

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:38.160
Just with each in breath, very gently noticing that whole area slightly extend and expand.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:46.240
And with each out breath, letting that whole area soften and be at ease.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.040
.

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:30.260
And now add in the neck and throat and the head.

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:49.060
So with each breath, just feeling the whole body be energized, be filled.

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:58.920
And then with each out breath feeling it get softer.

00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:15.140
Just a sense from the top of your head down through your torso all the way to your feet.

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:32.780
And you might even see if you can feel the breath extend slightly beyond what feels like

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:37.280
the edges of your body, out to the very edges of your skin.

00:22:55.800 --> 00:23:07.020
And from this place, now try and take three deep breaths and then see if you want to smile.

00:23:54.280 --> 00:23:56.440
And just notice how you feel now.

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:03.000
How it felt different to do that movement at the end of this exercise.

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:15.740
how the same movement, the same action probably felt quite different the three different times

00:24:15.740 --> 00:24:26.560
that we did it. And that leaves room for curiosity or openness that the way something impacts

00:24:26.560 --> 00:24:28.460
you might change and be different.

00:24:31.740 --> 00:24:34.480
As we are starting to come out of the meditation,

00:24:35.020 --> 00:24:38.000
just briefly reflecting on how this sit was for you.

00:24:45.840 --> 00:24:50.980
Knowing that if you want to, you can use this way of starting your meditation

00:24:51.600 --> 00:24:53.140
every time that you sit down.

00:24:53.140 --> 00:24:59.520
and that having the same thing that you do at the beginning of every sit can be really grounding.

00:25:04.560 --> 00:25:11.420
And now you can just gently start to come back into the room and open your eyes.
